            <!-- Full Policy Sub-tab -->
            <div id="prefectPolicySubTab" class="tab-content">
                <div class="card">
                    <h2 class="prefect-header">📜 Full Prefect Policy (2025 Update)</h2>
                    <div style="max-height:600px;overflow-y:auto;padding-right:10px;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.7;color:#334155;">
                        <h3 style="color:var(--prefect-color);margin-top:0;">1. Role of the Prefects Coordinator</h3>
                        <p>The Prefects Coordinator serves as the central point of contact for all matters concerning prefects at Surrey Primary School. Their responsibilities include:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Overseeing the selection process of prefects.</li>
                            <li>Providing training and ongoing support to prefects.</li>
                            <li>Developing and implementing policies and procedures related to prefects.</li>
                            <li>Liaising with school staff to ensure the effective functioning of the prefect system.</li>
                            <li>Addressing any issues or concerns raised by prefects or staff members.</li>
                            <li>Evaluating the performance of prefects and providing feedback for improvement.</li>
                            <li>Organising regular meetings with prefects to discuss upcoming events and responsibilities.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <h3 style="color:var(--prefect-color);">2. Selection Criteria and Process for Prefects</h3>
                        <p>Prefects are selected based on an assessment of their academic achievements, behaviour, leadership potential, and commitment to serving the school community. The selection process involves several stages:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Interview conducted by the Prefects Coordinator and other relevant staff members.</li>
                            <li>Reference checks from teachers and other school staff members.</li>
                            <li>Evaluation of the candidate's involvement in extracurricular activities and contributions to the school community.</li>
                            <li>Relevant teachers conduct a meeting to assess the suitability of the prefects.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <h3 style="color:var(--prefect-color);">3. Selection Criteria for Head Boy and Head Girl</h3>
                        <p>The Head Boy and Head Girl are chosen from the pool of prefects based on their exceptional leadership qualities, integrity, and dedication to the school's values. In addition to meeting the criteria for prefect selection, candidates for these positions must demonstrate:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Strong communication and interpersonal skills.</li>
                            <li>Initiative and the ability to motivate their peers.</li>
                            <li>A track record of exemplary behaviour and academic performance.</li>
                            <li>A commitment to serving as positive role models for their fellow learners.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <h3 style="color:var(--prefect-color);">4. Signing of Prefect Contracts</h3>
                        <p>All prefects, including the Head Boy and Head Girl, must sign a formal contract upon selection. The contract outlines their roles, responsibilities, and commitments. By signing the contract, prefects affirm their understanding of and dedication to their duties. Copies of these contracts are kept on record by the school administration.</p>
                        <p>The contract includes:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Detailed descriptions of duties and responsibilities.</li>
                            <li>A commitment to uphold the values and rules of the school.</li>
                            <li>Acknowledgement of the consequences of failing to meet expectations.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>The Head Boy and Head Girl have additional terms in their contracts, reflecting their enhanced leadership roles and responsibilities.</p>

                        <h3 style="color:var(--prefect-color);">5. Duties and Responsibilities of Prefects</h3>
                        <p>Prefects play a crucial role in maintaining discipline, fostering a positive school environment, and supporting the welfare of their peers. Their duties include:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Monitoring student behaviour and intervening when necessary to maintain order.</li>
                            <li>Assisting teachers and staff during assemblies, events, and other school activities.</li>
                            <li>Providing guidance and support to younger students.</li>
                            <li>Acting as mentors and advocates for their peers.</li>
                            <li>Participating in leadership training and development opportunities provided by the school.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <h3 style="color:var(--prefect-color);">6. Wearing of the Prefect Badge</h3>
                        <p>Prefects are required to wear their designated prefect badge visibly while on duty or representing the school. The badge serves as a symbol of their authority and responsibility within the school community, and its consistent display is mandatory. <strong>The purchasing of the prefect badge will be at the cost of the learner.</strong></p>

                        <h3 style="color:var(--prefect-color);">7. Distribution and Adherence to Prefect Duty Roster</h3>
                        <p>The Prefect's Coordinator is responsible for creating a detailed duty roster that assigns specific responsibilities to each prefect on a weekly basis. The roster includes information on duty times, locations, and tasks assigned to each prefect. Prefects are expected to:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Familiarise themselves with their assigned duties and responsibilities.</li>
                            <li>Arrive punctually at their designated duty stations and remain vigilant throughout their shifts.</li>
                            <li>Notify the Prefects Coordinator in advance if they are unable to fulfil their duties due to illness or other legitimate reasons.</li>
                            <li>Communicate effectively with fellow prefects and school staff to ensure the smooth coordination of duties.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <h3 style="color:var(--prefect-color);">8. Consequences for Prefects Who Do Not Fulfill Their Duties</h3>
                        <p>Prefects are held to high standards of conduct and professionalism, and failure to fulfil their duties may result in disciplinary action. The consequences for non-compliance include:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><span class="consequence-level verbal">Verbal warning</span> and counselling by the Prefects Coordinator.</li>
                            <li><span class="consequence-level written">Written warning</span> detailing the specific issues and expectations for improvement.</li>
                            <li><span class="consequence-level privilege">Removal from certain privileges or duties</span>, depending on the severity of the infraction.</li>
                            <li><span class="consequence-level suspension">Temporary suspension or demotion</span> from the position of prefect.</li>
                            <li><span class="consequence-level removal">Permanent removal</span> from the prefect team, if the behaviour persists despite intervention efforts.</li>
                            <li><span class="consequence-level referral">Referral to school leadership</span> for further disciplinary action, if deemed necessary.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>The Prefects Coordinator works closely with school leadership and relevant stakeholders to address any issues and provide support to prefects who may be struggling to meet their responsibilities. The goal is to foster a culture of accountability, integrity, and teamwork among the prefects, ultimately enhancing the overall effectiveness of the school's disciplinary and leadership systems.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
